  "result": "Perfect! All 142 tests pass. I've successfully added payment terms support:\n\n**Features added:**\n\n1. **Payment Terms** - createInvoice now accepts optional `terms` parameter\n   - `NET14`: Due 14 days after issue date\n   - `NET30`: Due 30 days after issue date (default)\n   - `EOM`: Due on last day of issue date's month\n   - Invalid terms return `TERMS_INVALID`\n\n2. **getLastDayOfMonth(date)** - new utility in src/dates.js\n   - Takes YYYY-MM-DD date\n   - Returns last day of that month in YYYY-MM-DD format\n   - UTC-based, leap year aware\n   - Example: `getLastDayOfMonth('2026-02-15')` \u2192 `'2026-02-28'`\n\n3. **Invoice Structure** - now includes:\n   - `terms`: Payment term code (NET14, NET30, or EOM)\n   - `dueDate`: Calculated based on terms (YYYY-MM-DD)\n   - Both stored on draft invoice\n\n4. **Date Calculations**\n   - NET14: uses `addDays(issueDate, 14)`\n   - NET30: uses `addDays(issueDate, 30)`\n   - EOM: uses `getLastDayOfMonth(issueDate)`\n\n**Test coverage (15 new tests):**\n- Default terms (NET30)\n- NET14 due date calculation\n- NET30 due date calculation\n- EOM due date calculation\n- Month-end dates (Jan 31, Apr 30, Dec 31)\n- Leap year February (2024-02-29)\n- Non-leap year February (2025-02-28)\n- Invalid terms rejection (case-sensitive)\n- All 12 months handled correctly\n\nAll terms stored with invoices and preserved through issuing process.",
